# S0: the FIRST job of the window: take production down. status lists the four boards (one firmware bundle, free hugepages, disk), agentstop stops the
# host's node agent and with it the serving container it started, and unserve removes any platform serving container that is left, so no
# serving process holds a card. PRODUCTION IS LIVE ON THE CARDS when the window opens: before this job the placement is removed through the admin API
# (the owner's go-ahead and an admin token); until then the agent reloads the container within minutes. No card is opened here.
# Read: four boards enumerate, the serving container is gone, no holders, at least 4 free 1 GiB hugepages, enough disk (the profile output guard stops at 85%).
# STOP on any failure: the window does not start with a card still held.
# Duration (estimate): 10 to 15 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next-3-scope window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-3-scope and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image a build-only job (C2_ACTIONS=build, no card opened) builds from this branch while
# production serves; a later commit of scripts needs a new build and tag. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3s is a PLACEHOLDER the driver may substitute.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status agentstop unserve
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3s
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
